	"note": "The NTA each LGU reported receiving, in pesos, from the Bureau of Local Government Finance’s Statement of Receipts and Expenditures (line “National Tax Allotment”) — a DOF figure, not a DBM one. DBM sets each share but publishes only BARMM-wide totals by level; BLGF is the only published per-LGU source. It is the LGU’s own share: barangay NTA is paid to the barangays and is not included, so there is no barangay figure. Cross-check: for FY 2025 the five provinces and three cities here sum to DBM’s BARMM provincial and city totals in LBM 90-A to the peso. FY 2025 is BLGF’s preliminary release; a few towns reported part-year receipts (Datu Hoffer Ampatuan’s FY 2025 is about a fifth of its FY 2024). A town that reported zero did not file — that year is left out, not written as 0. The eight Special Geographic Area towns, created in 2024, have no SRE rows yet. No per-LGU figure for FY 2026 is published by anyone yet.",
